aude Code did not load its part that starts the browser helper. Type /${xQt} (if it tells you to run it with --force, do that), then /claude-test. If that changes nothing, the usual cause is another enabled Claude Test plugin. In /plugin, open the Installed tab. Leave ${kX} (builtin) on. If the tab lists another Claude Test plugin, disable that one. Then, or if there is none, restart Claude Code.`,Kr=`To start Claude Test, type /claude-test in the terminal where Claude Code is running. If that does not start it, or from Remote Control, type /${xQt} first, then /claude-test.`,Yr="Claude Test is still getting ready. Type /claude-test in a moment.";function qr(e){return`Claude Test cannot run in this session: another enabled plugin is also named claude-test and loads first: ${e}. Disable or uninstall that one on the Installed tab of /plugin. Leave ${kX} (builtin) on. Then restart Claude Code.`}var Fe="Claude Test's browser helper is not ready in this session. Type /claude-test to start it and run the tests.",Jr="Claude Test could not start its test agent in this session, so nothing ran. Type /claude-test to try again. If this message comes back, restart Claude Code.",jt=`Claude Test did not start: its test agents are not loaded in this session. Type /${xQt} (if it tells you to run it with --force, do that), then /claude-test. If this message comes back, restart Claude Code.`,Wt="Claude Test did not start: its test agents are still loading. Type /claude-test in a moment.",Zr="Claude Test did not start: its test agents were loaded just now. Type /claude-test to run it.",dt="Claude Test is not available in this session right now, so it did not run. If you just changed your login, wait a moment, then type /claude-test again. If you see this message again, restart Claude Code; if it still shows, Claude Test is not available here.",ut="Claude Test did not run: the Claude Code login or plan changed since its browser helper started, or could not be checked, so the helper was s