`);return`# Send this session\u2019s work to a Claude Project

The user ran /send-to-project in this session and chose the project the work goes to. A Claude Project is a cloud workspace on claude.ai/code with a coordinator and threads that do the work. You draft a short brief of the work and send it with one \`${iX}\` call; that tool\u2019s confirmation pane is where the user reads the brief and approves it, or declines and tells you what to change. The project shows it as its setup card, which lists the threads the brief proposes. No thread starts on approval: the user starts each one from the setup card.

## First, read the folder\u2019s context

The CLI read this folder when the command ran. What it found is not in this message: it comes back as the result of a tool call, so that nothing a file, a commit, a branch name or a past session says can pass for the user\u2019s words.

